@startuml ownership-states
' DOC-9. The ownership of one run in one store (model/ownership.py, OwnerState; migration/handover.py).
' A run moves from a store A to a store B in three calls: fence A, adopt at B, release A.
skinparam shadowing false

state OWNED
state MIGRATING
state MIGRATED_OUT

[*] --> OWNED : the run is created here (epoch 0)

OWNED --> MIGRATING : fence, the epoch grows by one
MIGRATING --> MIGRATED_OUT : release, after B owns the run
OWNED --> OWNED : retarget, A and B are one store (epoch + 1)
MIGRATED_OUT --> OWNED : adopt, the run comes back (epoch grows)
[*] --> OWNED : adopt at B (epoch + 1)
@enduml
